\subsection{E1: Scalability}

Registration throughput scales linearly up to 10,000 identities measured
(34.7~ms/identity on quiet machine; 235.6~ms/identity on the loaded
benchmark host). Credential issuance latency is 5.4~ms P99 (SM2 tier,
quiet machine) at 208~TPS throughput, with delegation chain verification at 51.7~ms for 10 hops
(quiet) and 80.8~ms for 3 hops (loaded host). Revocation latency is
460~ms P99 (full accumulator snapshot bottleneck, quiet machine).
On the loaded host, SM2 credential verify measures 68.2~ms median
(14.6$\times$ the quiet baseline of 4.66~ms), confirming the load
contamination noted in~\S\ref{sec:setup}. Credential size is 449~B for
the SM2 tier, 12,989~B for the hybrid tier, and 608~B for the SLH-DSA
tier (wire JSON).

